  m_Name: 1400 malay
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Malay Settlements 14th-15th Century
  info: As a key part of the Malay Archipelago, Singapore saw the growth of Malay
    settlements. These communities contributed to the local language and traditions,
    such as kampong-style living and the spread of Islam. Malay culture remains central
    to Singapore's identity, reflected in architecture, art, and customs like Hari
    Raya celebrations.
